{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfBRbrwk77XBncwdUV5Cn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I submitted **index 0 (Fe 0.81, Sb 0.19)** as the best composition. At 0.055%, it had the highest external quantum efficiency (EQE) of the three I measured.\n\n- **Crystal structure (XRD):** I scanned indices 0, 5, 12 and 20. All four show the same main peaks. Index 20 (the Sb-rich end) also has one weak extra peak. Since the structure barely changes along the line, it gave no reason to pick one composition over another.\n- **EQE:** it went up steadily as the Fe fraction increased:\n\n| Index | Fe fraction | EQE (%) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 12 | 0.51 | 0.005 |\n| 5 | 0.71 | 0.014 |\n| 0 | 0.81 | 0.055 |\n\nBecause of that trend, I spent the last merit measurement on the most Fe-rich composition, and it came out best by about 4×.\n\nI can't tell whether EQE peaks just short of the Fe-rich end, since the library stops at Fe 0.81 and indices 1–4 were never measured. The Sb-rich half (Fe below 0.5) was also never measured. I skipped it because EQE was falling as Sb increased.\n\nI used all 3 merit measurements and 4 of the 5 XRD scans."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":508,"cache_read_input_tokens":8869,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":508},"output_tokens":434,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c48be511-8d56-4ae1-8f1c-a08c6a086542","uuid":"c87d5052-6524-48d3-8f6a-d443d6d71cd7","timestamp":"2026-09-18T19:04:03.965Z","request_id":"req_011CfBRbrSymSRYNWD1j8VhX"}
